"""Read-only analysis of the five completed RESUME X2 cohorts; no engine changes."""
from pathlib import Path
import csv,json,re,collections,zipfile
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
BASE=ROOT/'gauntlet/versions/jace'
SPECS=[('A','v0.1-real','2026-10-291734-smart-politics-100'),('B','v0.2-six','2026-10-292038-smart-politics-100'),('C','v0.2-six','2026-10-292338-smart-politics-keeptokens-50'),('D','v0.5-topdeck-tokens','2026-10-292338-smart-politics-keeptokens-50'),('E','v0.6-precon-engine','2026-10-300012-smart-politics-keeptokens-10')]
cfg=json.loads((ROOT/'gauntlet/gauntlet.json').read_text());pods={p['id']:p for p in cfg['pods']}
runs=[]
for label,v,rid in SPECS:
 p=BASE/v/'runs'/rid
 assert not any((p/n).exists() for n in ['INVALID.txt','ABORTED.txt'])
 s=json.loads((p/'summary.json').read_text());rows={r['card']:r for r in csv.DictReader((p/'card-stats.csv').open())};games=[]
 for f in sorted((p/'logs').glob('*.log')):
  text=f.read_text();result=re.search(r'^Game Result:.*$',text,re.M);assert result
  winner=re.search(r'Ai\((\d)\)-([^ ]+) has won',result[0]);ms=re.search(r'(?:ended in |Took )(\d+) ms',result[0]);timed=bool(ms and int(ms[1])>=599000)
  pid=f.name.split('-')[0];opp=pods[pid]['opponents'];wid=winner[2][3:] if winner and winner[2].startswith('b3-') else None
  games.append(dict(file=f,pod=pid,opponents=opp,win=bool(winner and winner[1]=='1'),winner=wid,timed=timed,text=text))
 assert len(games)==s['games'] and sum(g['win'] for g in games)==s['wins']
 runs.append(dict(label=label,v=v,id=rid,path=p,s=s,rows=rows,games=games))
L=['# Jace — analysis of finished runs','', 'Prepared 2026-10-29 by Codex for RESUME X2. These are Forge AI results, not predictions of Patrick’s human win rate. No new games or engine changes.','', '## What the evidence supports','', '- Keep the removal-first direction, but do not call the token package a proven upgrade. The directly relevant token-preserving runs are v0.2 16/50 (32%) and v0.5 18/50 (36%); two extra wins do not separate them. v0.6’s 5/10 is only a promising quick check.', '- Preserve Patrick’s keepers: Dreamtide Whale, Massacre Wurm, Triplicate Titan and Loyal Tutor. Small samples and AI limitations do not justify reversing those decisions.', '- Toxic Deluge, Sunfall, Synthetic Destiny and Overwrite the Multiverse are AI-piloting concerns. Do not describe them as bad real-life cards based on these runs.', '- The simulation reporter can label timeout games as wins. Historical headline rates below are reproduced faithfully; the separate sensitivity column removes those ambiguous winner credits by treating the suspect games as non-wins (draws). Claude should investigate before making final purchase claims.','', '## Cohorts and data quality','', '| Cohort | Version | Keep tokens | Reported wins | 95% Wilson interval | Suspect timeouts (Jace credits) | Wins if suspect games are draws |','|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|']
for r in runs:
 s=r['s'];t=[g for g in r['games'] if g['timed']];tw=sum(g['win'] for g in t)
 L.append(f"| {r['label']} | {r['v']} | {'yes' if s.get('keepTokens',False) else 'no'} | {s['wins']}/{s['games']} ({s['winRate']:.0%}) | {s['ci95'][0]:.1%}–{s['ci95'][1]:.1%} | {len(t)} ({tw}) | {s['wins']-tw}/{s['games']} ({(s['wins']-tw)/s['games']:.0%}) |")
L+=['', 'The intervals above are the original nominal binomial intervals. Fixed pods, repeated seeds and AI trajectories limit independence. A 50-game run gives three games in pods 01–10 and two in pods 11–20; a 100-game run gives five in every pod. A 10-game run covers only pods 01–10. Do not pool different deck versions, flags, or nested same-seed quick runs as independent evidence. A/B lack KEEP_TOKENS; older summaries omit the field, and their run names confirm it was absent.','', 'The 44% v0.2 headline becomes 40% in this timeout sensitivity check, while 32% becomes 26% for its token-preserving 50-game run. These are different settings and sample sizes; the gap does not isolate an effect of keeping tokens. C/D become 26% versus 36% under this sensitivity rule, which still does not establish superiority.','', 'Excluded: every run folder with INVALID.txt or ABORTED.txt, including v0.2 35% and v0.3 17% with the reverted Jace planeswalker-fodder change. Other quick runs, unfinished C1 runs and replays are outside this fixed five-cohort analysis. history.csv contains invalid rows and is not sufficient by itself.','', '### Timeout evidence for Lane C','', 'Threshold for this diagnostic: elapsed runtime >=599,000 ms. This flags suspicious games, not a claim that every long natural finish is invalid. `PodSim.java` sets a 600-second timeout and attempts `setGameOver(Draw)`, but actual log outcomes can contradict that intent. For example B/pod18-g3.log lists all four players as having won, followed by a single Jace winner in Game Result. `gauntlet.js` counts that final line as a Jace win. No source logs or summaries were modified.','']
for r in runs:
 t=[g for g in r['games'] if g['timed']]
 if t:L.append(f"- {r['label']}: "+'; '.join(g['file'].name+(' (Jace credited)' if g['win'] else ' (opponent credited)') for g in t))
L+=['','## Card interpretation','', '“Seen” below means recorded in a hand snapshot OR cast/land-played in the game; it is not the number of draw events. “Cast” means games with at least one cast, not total copies or activations. Jace −3 puts cards onto the battlefield without casting them, so low cast counts for expensive creatures can miss their main job. Win rates conditional on drawing or casting a card are associations: surviving long enough, matchup and board state all affect them.','', '### Cards to keep watching','', '- **Serra’s Emissary:** A wins 17/24 games where cast (70.8%); B 16/20 (80%). D is only 3/7 (42.9%). Strong historical signal, but not uniformly strong in every sample.', '- **Avacyn, Angel of Horror:** B 14/20 cast games won (70%); D 6/7 (85.7%); E 4/4. Supports keeping the payoff, with tiny later denominators.', '- **Cyclonic Rift:** B cast in 28/34 seen games, D 12/12. Forge does use it reliably. The package tests do not isolate its incremental value or prove that its price premium is worthwhile.', '- **Wrath of God / Infernal Grasp:** B cast 20/29 and 24/34 respectively; D 12/16 and 11/15. Both are operational in the AI and address the immediate survival problem.', '- **Chandra’s Ignition:** B cast 12/39 seen, with 3/12 wins when cast; D 9/21, with 4/9 wins. This is a conditional wipe needing a creature, not a uniformly top-performing card in the requested data. Earlier package-level improvement does not prove this individual card caused it.', '- **Dreamtide Whale:** A seen 36/cast 22; D 14/9. D wins 6/9 cast games. No basis for cutting Patrick’s keeper.', '- **Massacre Wurm / Triplicate Titan:** D cast 6/19 and 8/20 seen; wins 3/6 and 6/8 cast games. Expensive payoff cast rates are not sufficient cut criteria; Jace hits are not casts.', '- **Loyal Tutor:** A 28/40 seen, D 15/23, E 2/3 cast. It is being cast, but logs do not establish that the AI makes Patrick’s intended top-deck setup.', '- **Way of the Healer / Plan for All Outcomes:** D cast 8/18 each; neither has a clean repeated failure signal. Review opportunity cost in real play, rather than declaring them cuts from conditional win rates.', '', '### AI limitations: exclude from real-card rankings','']
for name in ['Toxic Deluge','Sunfall','Synthetic Destiny','Overwrite the Multiverse','Brainstone','Clever Concealment','Aetherize']:
 vals=[]
 for r in runs:
  row=r['rows'].get(name)
  if row:vals.append(f"{r['label']} {row['games_cast']}/{row['games_drawn']}")
 L.append(f"- **{name}:** cast/seen: "+'; '.join(vals)+'.')
L+=['', '**New finding:** Overwrite the Multiverse has zero casts across all five cohorts (124 game-exposures, not independent trials). Its local script has no RemoveDeck flag; zero use is still a practical piloting failure worth investigating. This is not evidence the real card is weak. Brainstone is actually cast in 10/17 seen games in D, contradicting the blanket “never casts” note. Casting an artifact does not prove the AI uses its draw/top-deck ability correctly. Preserve the limitation on judging its intended strategy until activations and choices are audited. Reactive protection/bounce can also look weak because the AI rarely holds mana; low Aetherize/Clever Concealment cast rates are not clean cut signals.','', 'Cards absent from these five cohorts (Soothsaying, Settle the Wreckage, Kenrith’s Transformation, Chainer) have no new measurements here; retain the known AI caveats from AGENTS.md.','', '### v0.6 owned-spare package','', '| Card | Seen | Cast games | First-cast average round | Wins when cast |','|---|---|---|---|---|']
for name in ["Skrelv's Hive",'Dreadhorde Invasion','Darksteel Angel']:
 row=runs[-1]['rows'][name];L.append(f"| {name} | {row['games_drawn']} | {row['games_cast']} | {row['avg_round_cast']} | {float(row['wr_cast']):.0%} |")
L+=['', 'These counts establish very little about package strength. Skrelv’s Hive makes Mites that cannot block: they feed Jace but do not satisfy the blocking half of the token plan. Dreadhorde’s Army grows beyond the current sim’s power-2 exile limit, so its real-life flexibility is understated. Darksteel Angel is a high-cost payoff; check actual entry-to-battlefield logs as well as casting before judging it.','', '## Who wins against Jace','', 'Each cell is **opponent wins / games that opponent appeared in**. This is a four-player result, not a head-to-head loss rate. Jace can lose to someone else in the same pod. Opponent archetypes come from gauntlet.json. These counts reproduce reported results, including flagged timeouts.','', '| Opponent | A | B | C | D | E |','|---|---|---|---|---|---|']
for oid,name in cfg['decks'].items():
 cells=[]
 for r in runs:
  den=sum(oid in g['opponents'] for g in r['games']);num=sum(g['winner']==oid for g in r['games']);cells.append(f'{num}/{den}')
 L.append('| '+name+' | '+' | '.join(cells)+' |')
L+=['', '### How the losses happen','', 'Winner counts alone do not reveal the killing blow. The examples below are log evidence, not an automated attribution of every loss.','', '- **Ghalta explosive combat:** E/pod03-g1.log records Jace losing to life total zero; Vaultborn Tyrant alone deals 56 combat damage to Jace, Surrak and Goreclaw 48, and Hulking Raptor 48. This is a wide, amplified army as well as a huge-trample problem. A single exile answer may buy time but cannot replace all board wipes.', '- **Control:** Yennett wins the most opposing games in B (14) and is second in C (5, behind Arcades’s 6). Its control label describes the deck, not a demonstrated cause for each individual loss. D/pod01-g3.log shows a combat finish with Serra’s Emissary dealing 7, Magister Sphinx 5 and Yennett 3 damage to Jace, who loses to life total zero. D’s leading opposing winner is Giada (7), followed by Ghalta (6) and Yennett (5); the earlier “Yennett always leads upgraded lists” shorthand does not hold for every cohort.', '- **Flying pressure:** Giada is the baseline’s most frequent opposing winner (13/25 appearances), and D’s (7/12). D/pod07-g1.log verifies a combat loss: Sigarda’s Vanguard and Angelic Sell-Sword each deal 8 damage to Jace, Serra Paragon 5, Linvala 4 and Giada 2; Jace loses to life total zero. This supports flying-army pressure in that example, not an attribution for every Giada win.', '- **No universal worst matchup is established:** Ghalta’s worst-matchup reputation is relevant for targeted testing, but these five winner tables do not prove it is the worst under every list. Pod composition and a different opponent winning complicate such a ranking.', '', '## Full per-card comparison','', 'All cards present in the cohort CSVs, including lands. Cell = **seen / cast-or-played games; win rate when cast-or-played**. “—” means absent from that cohort’s CSV. “n/a” means zero cast games. Land plays appear in the same source column as casts. These are source CSV values, without pooling or causal ranking.','', '| Card | A | B | C | D | E |','|---|---|---|---|---|---|']
for name in sorted(set().union(*(r['rows'] for r in runs))):
 cells=[]
 for r in runs:
  row=r['rows'].get(name)
  cells.append('—' if row is None else f"{row['games_drawn']}/{row['games_cast']}; "+(f"{float(row['wr_cast']):.1%}" if row['wr_cast'] else 'n/a'))
 L.append('| '+name+' | '+' | '.join(cells)+' |')
L+=['', '## Sources and reproducibility','', 'Generated with `python3 analysis/jace-finished-runs.py`. Each input run was checked for invalid/aborted markers, completed summary, exact log count and agreement between logged Jace wins and summary. The source card CSVs retain additional columns: first-cast round and seen/not-seen conditional win rates.','']
for r in runs:L.append(f"- {r['label']}: [{r['v']} / {r['id']}]({r['v']}/runs/{r['id']}/summary.json); [card CSV]({r['v']}/runs/{r['id']}/card-stats.csv).")
L+=['', 'Engine interpretation checked against `gauntlet/gauntlet.js`, `forge/replaysim/src/forge/view/PodSim.java`, `forge/custom/CHANGELOG.md` and local Forge card scripts. Recommendations await Claude’s completed C1 comparison and C3 targeted-answer test.']
(BASE/'ANALYSIS.md').write_text('\n'.join(L)+'\n')
print('Wrote ANALYSIS.md:',len(L),'lines')
print('Overwrite seen total',sum(int(r['rows']['Overwrite the Multiverse']['games_drawn']) for r in runs))
